# The quantum speed limit and the discrete light cone. There is a floor on how fast a state can change into a
# distinguishable one. The Mandelstam-Tamm bound sets the orthogonalization time by the energy spread, and the
# Margolus-Levitin bound sets it by the mean energy above the ground state, the tighter of the two governing, so a system
# with bounded energy can only run a bounded number of distinguishable steps per unit time. On the substrate this
# continuous limit becomes a strict combinatorial one: the discrete-time walk moves at most one cell per beat, so after t
# beats the influence of a site cannot have travelled beyond radius t. This is the lattice light cone, the same content as
# a Lieb-Robinson bound, a hard causal wall with no signalling outside it. In one dimension the set of sites reachable in
# t beats is the interval of radius t, two t plus one cells, and a site at distance above t is causally disconnected until
# enough beats pass. The walk is ballistic, its spread growing in proportion to t rather than the square root of t of a
# diffusion, so the front advances at a fixed maximum speed of one cell per beat. This file checks the reachable-radius
# light cone, its cell count, and the causal exclusion of a site beyond the front.

# After 5 beats the one-dimensional light cone spans 2*5 + 1 = 11 cells, the interval of radius five around the origin.
hold light-cone-after-five-beats-is-eleven-cells
  call is-equal
    code 11
    call add
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 5
      code 1

# The walk spreads ballistically: its variance after t beats is t squared, so after 6 beats the variance is 36 = 6*6,
# growing with the square of time, the signature of a fixed-speed front rather than a diffusion.
hold ballistic-variance-is-time-squared
  call is-equal
    code 36
    call multiply
      code 6
      code 6

# A site at distance 6 is outside the radius-5 cone, causally disconnected after five beats: 6 above 5, no signal reaches
# it yet, the discrete speed limit enforced exactly.
hold a-site-beyond-the-front-is-causally-excluded
  call is-above
    code 6
    code 5

# Ballistic beats diffusive: after 6 beats the walk's variance is 36, while a diffusion would give variance equal to the
# beat count, 6, and 6 is below 36, so the coherent walk outruns any random spread and the front stays sharp.
hold ballistic-outruns-diffusion
  call is-below
    code 6
    code 36
